name: sim.createPrimitiveShape
description: Creates a primitive shape
luaSynopsis: int shapeHandle = sim.createPrimitiveShape(int primitiveType, list sizes, int options = 0)
pythonSynopsis: int shapeHandle = sim.createPrimitiveShape(int primitiveType, float[3] sizes, int options = 0)
inputs:
1. primitiveType: the primitive type of the shape
2. sizes: 3 values indicating the size of the shape
3. options: Bit-coded:
    - bit0 is set (1): backfaces are culled
    - bit1 is set (2): edges appear sharp
    - bit2 is set (4): cylinder has open ends
    - bit3 is set (8): the primitive shape is not registered as such by CoppeliaSim, but rather as a random (maybe convex) shape
outputs:
1. shapeHandle: handle of the newly created shape
